  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Capacity Building of ACADES</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">ACADES: Sector Agriculture (cassava), Beneficiaries: 330 farmers, including 147 women, ACADES is a youth owned association that was established by graduate agriculturalist who resorted into farming when they could not get employed after graduating. They decided to work with other young people who are interested in agribusiness. They mobilized the farmers as their objective is to ensure that these young farmers have adequate quality inputs as well as access to profitable markets. They are working with farmers from Mchinji and Lilongwe rural with possibility of expanding to other districts later as they grow. Several NGO&apos;s and government departments like the National Youth Council are supporting this initiative.</narrative>
  </description>
